    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d578">

                <pb facs="0761" n="753" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg753"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/1519²⁄₄</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to
                        the British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Halifax</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-14">December 14,
                        1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Halifax</hi>: Here is a message to General
                    Chiang Kai-Shek<anchor n="63" xml:id="d578-f1"/> and a similar message from me
                    to Mr. Stalin.<anchor n="64" xml:id="d578-f2"/> They are self-explanatory.</p>
                <p>I hope you will ask London if they will go ahead with the holding of the
                    Singapore conference and also instruct your people in Chungking and Moscow to
                    take part in the proposed meetings as soon as they are held by Chiang Kai-Shek
                    and Stalin. I assume, of course, that Australia and New Zealand will be
                    represented in Singapore.</p>
                <p>Always sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Franklin D. Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
